- Use ESLint for static code analysis and maintaining code quality standards.
- Configure ESLint with appropriate presets for your project type (React, Node.js, etc.).
- Implement custom ESLint rules for project-specific coding standards.
- Use ESLint plugins for framework-specific linting (React, Vue, Angular).
- Integrate ESLint with your IDE for real-time code quality feedback.
- Configure ESLint to work with Prettier for code formatting consistency.
- Use ESLint's autofix capabilities to automatically resolve common issues.
- Set up ESLint in CI/CD pipeline to enforce code quality in pull requests.
- Create comprehensive ESLint configuration files with proper rule inheritance.
- Use ESLint overrides for different file types and environments.

